     "body": "<p>Adding some noise here + 2 Cents : I know <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Afe14f014-ccfb-4882-b081-85802f8c5346\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"557058:fe14f014-ccfb-4882-b081-85802f8c5346\" data-account-id=\"557058:fe14f014-ccfb-4882-b081-85802f8c5346\" accountid=\"557058:fe14f014-ccfb-4882-b081-85802f8c5346\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Nick Ruest</a> is working on this, and since i'm doing some internal research on the Islandora world i was thinking maybe we could move this to an upper level (in terms of where do we enforce, what do we expose) + how we also allow all different rdf sources (triple stores, dumps, whatever) to play together by enabling webAC to be enforced on query time in a transparent manner.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"http://ebiquity.umbc.edu/blogger/2015/04/19/access-control-for-a-triplestore-linked-data-fragments-interface/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://ebiquity.umbc.edu/blogger/2015/04/19/access-control-for-a-triplestore-linked-data-fragments-interface/</a><br/>\n<a href=\"http://linkeddatafragments.org\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://linkeddatafragments.org</a></p>\n\n<p>(Look at the software tab)</p>\n",
